{
 "voice": "Anchit, recreated with Chatterbox Multilingual (MIT licence) from Anchit's own recording",
 "lines": {
  "A few calm steps so you can answer from care, not from heat.": "1c9ee1f5e632",
  "A gentle self-compassion break for when your inner voice feels harsh.": "bd2f951dfcd7",
  "A little more": "c563b47bf9f7",
  "A plate is set beside you, still warm, and a glass of ginger tea.": "3140fe59a7a6",
  "A slow train waits at the platform, its windows glowing warm and yellow.": "57c478cf0a41",
  "A soft blanket is around your shoulders.": "b8ca70cc87a9",
  "A soft light rises over the hills and touches the water.": "408e0926055c",
  "A tea seller passes by, and you take a small cup of sweet, milky chai.": "1561a0df71fe",
  "Ask yourself: what do I need right now?": "d147118d7188",
  "Ask: what might they be feeling?": "a77658efb86a",
  "Ask: what would I say to a dear friend who felt this way? Say it to you.": "dcf8197f4dc1",
  "Both eyes. Both ears. The nose. The lips. The chin. The throat.": "4dd039f13ed7",
  "Box breathing: in for four, hold for four, out for four, rest for four.": "e089b3c92038",
  "Breathe in": "5f140e42337d",
  "Breathe out": "10f0411a9409",
  "Bring your attention to the top of your head.": "e37eb13f1847",
  "Bring your attention to your chest, rising and falling on its own.": "abb9fe79b5bd",
  "Choose one kind, honest sentence to begin with.": "4d0154fa99b4",
  "Clack, clack. Clack, clack. Slower now.": "b56920d51fc9",
  "Count each breath backwards from twenty-seven. Breathing in, twenty-seven. Breathing out, twenty-seven.": "80fbb17fa15a",
  "Drops gather at the edge of the roof and fall, one after another.": "da8d07f55ac0",
  "Each drop on the roof feels like a small, kind word.": "7cdc33a3ff78",
  "Feel that same stillness inside you.": "9a284eff6c5c",
  "Feel the weight of your upper arms, then your elbows, then your forearms.": "0248f47b914d",
  "Feel your back supported by the bed, all the way down.": "5cf78393ba77",
  "Feel your neck soften into the pillow.": "a08f271259e9",
  "Feel your thighs, then your knees, soften.": "3022834ecc96",
  "Find 2 things you can smell, or 2 favourite scents.": "10c65fb99f5b",
  "Gently notice the world around you, one sense at a time.": "531c35cbdaf9",
  "Get ready": "70c1b9f24067",
  "Hold gently": "f270be0dff8e",
  "If a thought comes, let it pass like a cloud, and come back to the body.": "23a9ae006eaf",
  "If the count slips away, gently begin again. There is no hurry.": "f80acd38f6ff",
  "In the garden, the leaves of the mango tree shine in the lamplight.": "231137f144d9",
  "It is evening, and the little station is almost empty.": "d4d1b426e777",
  "Left hand thumb. Second finger. Third finger. Fourth finger. Little finger.": "accc1282ce4e",
  "Left heel. Sole of the left foot. All the toes of the left foot.": "bf401d58a526",
  "Left side of the chest. Left hip. Left thigh. Knee. Calf. Ankle.": "517862dcf7e4",
  "Let the sound of the rain carry you gently into sleep.": "86809b07aa8c",
  "Let us begin. Sit comfortably, let your shoulders drop, and follow the sun as it opens and closes.": "39b7a9e0dd45",
  "Let us begin. Take your time with each step. There is no rush.": "4a4c47ce8890",
  "Let us begin. Type whatever is on your mind. Nothing is saved.": "36064e4560d0",
  "Let your belly be soft. There is nothing to hold in.": "d168fb62fe6e",
  "Let your body be still. This is a time to rest, not to sleep yet.": "b86c634e72f8",
  "Let your calves relax, and your ankles.": "67f858ab9a91",
  "Let your eyes close, or soften your gaze.": "0a8e4c786a3b",
  "Let your eyes grow heavy in their sockets.": "d790c5aacc66",
  "Let your forehead smooth out, and your eyebrows rest.": "308564eecf5e",
  "Let your hands rest open. Notice any warmth in your palms.": "ba435a38aa23",
  "Let your hips grow heavy.": "602b441fc843",
  "Let your jaw loosen. Your teeth can part a little.": "27b14865e49a",
  "Let your shoulders drop, a little more with each breath out.": "71f25a064aba",
  "Lie down comfortably and let your arms rest by your sides.": "054829bb7600",
  "Lie on your back in a comfortable position, palms facing up.": "e08fe3257183",
  "Lift your shoulders up to your ears. Hold. Let them drop.": "ecdc1c4756fc",
  "Listen for 3 sounds, near or far.": "b3e0d5fea110",
  "Long breath out": "8f4ebdc9dde9",
  "Long breaths out that help your body settle after a disagreement.": "434932071b54",
  "Look around and name 5 things you can see.": "0872b1dab554",
  "Look at something far away for twenty seconds.": "c345c257d58a",
  "Lovely. Take a moment to notice how you feel now.": "23ccb24582ce",
  "Make two fists. Squeeze. Open your hands wide and soft.": "d3d1336a6c2b",
  "Name it softly: this is a hard moment.": "38de4f2621e5",
  "Name the feeling in one word.": "8eafffe19f89",
  "Notice 1 taste, or take a sip of water.": "3cb89892bae1",
  "Notice 4 things you can feel, like your feet or your sleeves.": "2da8fda0980c",
  "Notice the sounds around you, far away and close by. Just listen.": "4074ffb00c25",
  "Notice your feet. Let your toes uncurl.": "bbeb6e8c7f1d",
  "Now choose a short, kind intention, a sankalpa. For example: I am at peace.": "a89d748b76e5",
  "Now feel your whole body at once, heavy and warm.": "73b813288515",
  "Now it is evening, and you are sitting on a wide, old verandah.": "15beb15bc13e",
  "Now notice the natural breath, without changing it.": "f80c9ab53e5d",
  "Now notice your body lying here, and the places it touches the bed.": "e4f391cd6919",
  "Now picture a calm lake at dawn, the water perfectly still.": "b48922079602",
  "Now picture the person you feel tense with.": "7c109ebac8ce",
  "Now remember your sankalpa, and repeat it three times, with feeling.": "e51a8c4d7fd7",
  "Now we move awareness through the body. Just feel each place as it is named.": "eeb62385effe",
  "On the other side, the sky is full of stars.": "6c10fa8774e0",
  "Outside, the town lights thin out, one by one, until there are only fields.": "887a78c52d0f",
  "Palm of the left hand. Back of the hand. Wrist. Elbow. Shoulder.": "86aa4ce4ddd4",
  "Palm of the right hand. Back of the hand. Wrist. Elbow. Shoulder.": "ed793741abf7",
  "Picture someone you care about and smile at them in your mind.": "be72c45a671d",
  "Pine trees stand along the track, dark and quiet.": "f36bf1ac2224",
  "Place a hand on your heart or your cheek. Feel its warmth.": "cbe2cffb3b45",
  "Press your feet into the floor. Then let them rest.": "939a997913bd",
  "Press your palms together for a breath, then let them go soft.": "0feabd7421e0",
  "Rain falls steadily on the tin roof above you.": "31f10489c961",
  "Release the workday from your body without leaving your chair.": "d7f0008a7ed7",
  "Remember: everyone has hard moments. You are not alone in this.": "6f982b9f8d35",
  "Repeat your sankalpa three times in your mind, with feeling.": "4661d94207c7",
  "Rest": "b79e5f48220d",
  "Rest here, and let sleep come when it is ready.": "92862cadd080",
  "Rest in this stillness. If sleep comes now, welcome it.": "986d64f065d0",
  "Right hand thumb. Second finger. Third finger. Fourth finger. Little finger.": "28a91e93da0b",
  "Right heel. Sole of the right foot. All the toes of the right foot.": "e0e53d126bfe",
  "Right side of the chest. Right hip. Right thigh. Knee. Calf. Ankle.": "8d54c3b9b777",
  "Roll your shoulders back slowly, five times.": "33369e49eab7",
  "Say to yourself: I am going to practise yoga nidra. I will stay aware.": "8fc619acf1c7",
  "Say to yourself: may I be kind to myself right now.": "8eb666e54029",
  "Scrunch your face. Then let your jaw hang loose.": "163c3ecc3c00",
  "Send kind wishes to someone you love, someone you feel tense with, and yourself.": "2d8f34852d9e",
  "Sit tall, feet flat, and take one long breath out.": "427be4faed05",
  "Sixty seconds of slow, easy breathing. Always free.": "396bca093c3e",
  "Small houses appear on the hillside, one lamp still lit in a window.": "b139939a451f",
  "Soft, even breathing. In for five, out for five, like a slow breeze.": "165950a9c87d",
  "Someone in the kitchen is making pakoras. You can hear the gentle sizzle.": "da00b9bfb47a",
  "Somewhere a frog begins to sing, and then another answers.": "f52f8ef6694c",
  "Somewhere below, a stream runs over smooth stones.": "7a1c9bac563b",
  "Take one long breath and feel your whole body settle.": "39c04301b708",
  "Take one slow breath before you say anything.": "ac75963baa62",
  "Take three slow breaths, longer on the way out.": "d228c70b52aa",
  "Tense each area for a breath, then let it go soft, from shoulders to toes.": "30808454c492",
  "The air coming in through the window grows cooler.": "1ac55a9d24ab",
  "The air smells of wet earth, that sweet smell the first rain brings.": "2faa7a4de0e9",
  "The back of the head. The forehead. Both eyebrows. The space between the eyebrows.": "b353b0eba21a",
  "The carriage sways gently, like a cradle.": "cffdf92430d6",
  "The fields are silver under a half moon.": "7c30796d7853",
  "The first rain of the monsoon arrived this afternoon.": "7bd45dda83db",
  "The lamp flickers, warm and steady.": "c81856485aab",
  "The rain softens to a gentle patter.": "b86682cebe77",
  "The street outside is quiet. Everyone has gone in.": "9cee60abf134",
  "The train begins to climb, slowly, curving around the first hill.": "a8e64714dc98",
  "The train passes through a short tunnel, and the sound grows soft and round.": "7ae568b386ab",
  "The wheels find their rhythm. Clack, clack. Clack, clack.": "a94eef935eeb",
  "The whistle sounds once, long and low, and the train begins to move.": "53c7145a9ce9",
  "The whole right side of the body. The whole left side. The whole body together.": "14e0710bd7e3",
  "There is nothing more to do now.": "18a42184f4f1",
  "There is nothing to do tonight but listen.": "1422eefd0d85",
  "There is nowhere you need to be. The train knows the way.": "8222e3d52839",
  "Tilt one ear toward your shoulder, then the other.": "fae14af87769",
  "Two easy breaths in through the nose, then one long, slow breath out.": "dece82ab6c0b",
  "Two minutes to type whatever is on your mind. Nothing is saved.": "5b8c865e1e41",
  "Voice guide on.": "fc89e2c3814b",
  "Wish them: may you feel safe and at ease.": "a7b4bc49c5b7",
  "Wish them: may you find some ease too.": "213b4ce8f16e",
  "Wish yourself the same: may I feel at ease.": "b3cd276646a0",
  "With each breath out, sink a little deeper into rest.": "633d24157161",
  "You eat slowly, and watch the rain.": "e2dfa14e4c15",
  "You find a seat by the window. The cushion is soft and a little worn.": "963bbf89a445",
  "You pull the blanket a little closer and lean back in the chair.": "83a354989ce4",
  "Your breathing slows to match the rain.": "10e3e7c4c8a0",
